106
00:30:19,000 --> 00:30:29,079
As you'll recall, the voters in 2018 legalized medical marijuana in the state of Oklahoma.

107
00:30:29,079 --> 00:30:34,470
And licenses started getting issued 30 days after that was done.

108
00:30:34,470 --> 00:30:42,150
It wasn't till over a year later in 2019, but the legislature passed legislation that

109
00:30:42,150 --> 00:30:49,349
allowed municipalities to regulate medical marijuana businesses and their communities.

110
00:30:49,349 --> 00:30:54,190
So by time we had the right to do that, we already had a bunch of businesses that were

111
00:30:54,190 --> 00:30:55,789
in place.

112
00:30:55,789 --> 00:31:02,980
And basically, under the law, they were grandfathered in, we were stuck with it.

113
00:31:02,980 --> 00:31:12,519
We did pass that first ordinance in 2019, but in 2020, the council at that time made

114
00:31:12,519 --> 00:31:23,519
it clear that they wanted to set aside the downtown district and try to not have medical

115
00:31:23,519 --> 00:31:25,819
marijuana businesses there.

116
00:31:25,819 --> 00:31:26,819
We already had a handful.

117
00:31:26,819 --> 00:31:30,940
There were a few that were already operating, and so we were kind of stuck with those.

118
00:31:30,940 --> 00:31:39,779
But at that time, they enacted an amendment to this ordinance that basically said there would

119
00:31:39,779 --> 00:31:45,099
be no new medical marijuana businesses in the downtown area.

120
00:31:45,099 --> 00:31:54,519
And downtown roughly is Steve Owens Boulevard to the railroad tracks from A Street to A Street.

121
00:31:54,519 --> 00:32:03,019
So it's a six block area that we're talking about.

122
00:32:03,019 --> 00:32:08,700
We authorized those businesses that were already in operation to continue in business.

123
00:32:08,700 --> 00:32:14,880
If we hadn't done that, we would have been sued and we would have lost on that.

124
00:32:14,880 --> 00:32:23,079
But we did put in provisions that if a business that's already there gets shut down, then they

125
00:32:23,079 --> 00:32:25,500
can't reopen.

126
00:32:25,500 --> 00:32:31,420
And so after the last meeting, the mayor of talk with me about that, and you wanted to make

127
00:32:31,420 --> 00:32:38,619
sure that we had that as tight as we could for the downtown area.

128
00:32:38,619 --> 00:32:40,900
That's all we're talking about is the downtown area.

129
00:32:40,900 --> 00:32:49,450
As you all know, we've got marijuana businesses all over town for further operations.

130
00:32:49,450 --> 00:32:55,009
And we did that ordinance in 2020.

131
00:32:55,009 --> 00:32:59,849
There was kind of best guess as to what issues may come up.

132
00:33:00,430 --> 00:33:11,430
Since then, we have had issues come up with one business in particular, and so we have a little bit more of a solid framework with which to assess our ordinance.

133
00:33:11,430 --> 00:33:18,430
And so with that in mind, I went back in, made some amendments to the ordinance.

134
00:33:18,430 --> 00:33:29,750
The red line copy that you all got, I think, first of all, reaffirms in doing this ordinance.

135
00:33:29,750 --> 00:33:40,779
You all are reaffirming the decision that you don't want medical marijuana businesses in the downtown area to the extent that we don't have to.

136
00:33:40,779 --> 00:33:50,460
And that if a business that is already there shuts down, then for whatever reason, they can't reopen.

137
00:33:50,460 --> 00:34:01,460
And under the state statute that we have, it's my opinion that we're valid in doing what we're doing.

138
00:34:01,460 --> 00:34:05,490
Basically, the ordinance says that we can regulate them through zoning.

139
00:34:05,490 --> 00:34:10,489
The only thing we can't do is just prohibit any medical marijuana business from the city.

140
00:34:10,489 --> 00:34:14,489
Well, obviously, we're not doing that, because we have mall over the city.

141
00:34:14,489 --> 00:34:20,489
It's just that we don't want them in that particular area of the city.

142
00:34:20,489 --> 00:34:25,489
And so, hence you have this ordinance in front of you.

143
00:34:25,489 --> 00:34:40,579
